  <h2>S Tier — Order Every Time</h2>

  <h3>1. Oreo® Cookie Blizzard — The GOAT</h3>
  <p>The <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Cookie Blizzard</a> is DQ's #1 best-seller for a reason. Real Oreo pieces blended evenly throughout vanilla soft serve — every spoonful has the same ratio from top to bottom. The flavor is perfectly calibrated between sweet and chocolatey, and the crunch is the best texture contrast on the Blizzard menu. From $3.49 Mini. If you have never had a Blizzard, start here.</p>

  <h3>2. Royal Oreo® Blizzard</h3>
  <p>Everything the standard Oreo Blizzard delivers, plus a warm hot fudge-filled center. The moment you hit the fudge pocket mid-cup changes the experience. The <a href="/items/royal-oreo-blizzard">Royal Oreo</a> costs about $1 more per size and earns it. From $3.99 Mini.</p>

  <h3>3. Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough Blizzard</h3>
  <p>The <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough Blizzard</a> is DQ's #2 best-seller. Chunky cookie dough pieces blended throughout soft serve — more textural variety per bite than any other core Blizzard. The large chunks are satisfying in a way fine crumbles are not. 590 cal Small. From $3.49.</p>

  <h2>A Tier — Excellent, Order Confidently</h2>

  <h3>4. Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup Blizzard</h3>
  <p>If you love peanut butter and chocolate, the <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's Blizzard</a> is the definitive option. Rich, intense, high-calorie (600 cal Small), and completely satisfying. Not for light eaters. From $3.49.</p>

  <h3>5. Royal Reese's® Blizzard</h3>
  <p>The <a href="/items/royal-reeses-blizzard">Royal Reese's</a> adds a warm peanut butter-filled center to the already-intense Reese's Blizzard. The highest-calorie Blizzard on the menu (620 cal Small), and arguably the most indulgent. From $3.99.</p>

  <h3>6. Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard</h3>
  <p>The <a href="/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard">Turtle Pecan Cluster</a> is the most texturally sophisticated year-round Blizzard — real pecans, caramel, and hot fudge. The only Blizzard that uses whole nuts as a primary mix-in. From $3.99. <em>Note: Contains tree nuts.</em></p>

  <h3>7. Swicy Pineapple with Tajín® Blizzard ⭐ Summer 2026 Pick</h3>
  <p>The boldest seasonal Blizzard DQ has launched. The <a href="/items/swicy-pineapple-tajin-blizzard">Swicy Pineapple Tajín</a> is genuinely surprising — the chili-lime seasoning builds heat that works beautifully with cold soft serve and sweet pineapple. The lightest-calorie Summer 2026 seasonal at 430 cal Small. Order it before it's gone.</p>

  <h2>B Tier — Great Choices, Personal Preference Dependent</h2>

  <h3>8. Snickers® Blizzard</h3>
  <p>The <a href="/items/snickers-blizzard">Snickers Blizzard</a> delivers four distinct elements per spoonful — peanuts, caramel, nougat, chocolate. The most complex candy-bar Blizzard. 500 cal Small. <em>Contains peanuts.</em></p>

  <h3>9. Choco Brownie Extreme Blizzard</h3>
  <p>For committed chocolate fans. The <a href="/items/choco-brownie-blizzard">Choco Brownie Extreme</a> uses actual baked brownie pieces — dark, chewy, intensely chocolatey. 510 cal Small. From $3.99.</p>

  <h3>10. S'mores Blizzard ☀️ Summer 2026</h3>
  <p>A reliable seasonal return. The <a href="/items/smores-blizzard">S'mores Blizzard</a> executes the campfire flavor combination well — graham cracker crunch, marshmallow sweetness, fudge depth. 500 cal Small. From $4.49.</p>

  <h3>11. Brownie Batter Blizzard</h3>
  <p>Softer and sweeter than Choco Brownie Extreme. The <a href="/items/brownie-batter-blizzard">Brownie Batter Blizzard</a> hits the unbaked dessert craving well. 530 cal Small. From $3.99.</p>

  <h3>12. Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake Blizzard ☀️ Summer 2026</h3>
  <p>The richest Summer 2026 seasonal at 540 cal Small. The <a href="/items/dipped-strawberry-cheesecake-blizzard">Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake</a> combines fruit, cheesecake, and fudge — a complex flavor that rewards patient eating. From $4.49.</p>

  <h2>C Tier — Good, But Specific Audience</h2>

  <h3>13. Butterfinger® Blizzard</h3>
  <p>Light, crispy peanut-butter wafer crunch. The <a href="/items/butterfinger-blizzard">Butterfinger Blizzard</a> (470 cal Small) is the best choice for guests who want a hint of peanut butter without the intensity of Reese's. From $3.49.</p>

  <h3>14. M&amp;M's® Blizzard</h3>
  <p>Colorful, crunchy, familiar. The <a href="/items/mm-blizzard">M&amp;M's Blizzard</a> is the top choice for kids. For adults who love M&amp;M's, it is a solid B. For everyone else, there are more interesting options at the same price. 490 cal Small. From $3.49.</p>

  <h3>15. Confetti Cake Blizzard ☀️ Summer 2026</h3>
  <p>Fun and festive. The <a href="/items/confetti-cake-blizzard">Confetti Cake Blizzard</a> (490 cal Small) is the right order for a birthday visit. Otherwise, it is sweet without much complexity. From $4.49.</p>

  <h3>16. Cotton Candy Blizzard ☀️ Summer 2026</h3>
  <p>The lightest Summer 2026 seasonal at 460 cal Small. The <a href="/items/cotton-candy-blizzard">Cotton Candy Blizzard</a> is exactly what it promises — simple, sweet, fair-food flavor. Best for kids and guests who want something light. From $4.49.</p>

  <h3>17. Royal New York Cheesecake Blizzard</h3>
  <p>The <a href="/items/royal-new-york-cheesecake-blizzard">Royal New York Cheesecake</a> (510 cal Small) is a well-executed fruity Royal Blizzard. The strawberry center adds a nice burst, but the overall flavor is more subtle than most guests expect from a "Royal." From $3.99.</p>

  <h3>18. Heath® Bar Blizzard</h3>
  <p>The <a href="/items/heath-blizzard">Heath Blizzard</a> (480 cal Small) is excellent if you love English toffee. If you are indifferent to toffee, there is no particular reason to choose it over Oreo or Cookie Dough. From $3.49. <em>Contains tree nuts (almonds).</em></p>

  <h2>Seasonal vs. Year-Round — What to Order When</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Year-round, always safe:</strong> Oreo, Cookie Dough, Reese's, Turtle Pecan Cluster</li>
    <li><strong>Summer 2026 — order now:</strong> Swicy Pineapple Tajín, S'mores, Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake</li>
    <li><strong>Fall 2026 (coming soon):</strong> Pumpkin Pie Blizzard returns in September</li>
    <li><strong>Winter 2026–27:</strong> Peppermint Hot Cocoa and Frosted Sugar Cookie Blizzards</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Bottom Line</h2>
  <p>The Oreo Blizzard is the correct default. Cookie Dough is the correct upgrade when you want something richer. Royal Oreo is the correct upgrade when you want to spend $1 more for a significantly better experience. Everything in A and B tier is genuinely good — the differences are personal preference, not quality. Browse the complete <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats lineup with 2026 prices</a> or return to <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a> for the full menu.</p>
